    "Synthetic sample. Every key, title, person and pull request here is made up;",
    "it exists to document the payload format and to give a new deployment",
    "something to render. Real payloads are gitignored — keep yours outside the",
    "repo and point the importer at it.",
    "",
    "It also shows the checkpoint rules the importer expects:",
    "  DEMO-104 carries resolvedAt, meaning it never entered Dev Done and took",
    "  its week from the Jira resolution date instead.",
    "  DEMO-107 has neither signal, so it sits in the backlog row.",
    "  W32 is declared but empty — a real week with nothing delivered, kept",
    "  visible rather than closed up.",
    "",
    "resolvedAt is provenance only. The importer (import-board.mjs) forwards ticket",
    "fields by name and never sends it to Convex."
